Intel OSPRay is an open source, scalable and portable ray tracing
engine for high-performance, high-fidelity visualization.  It provides
a C/C++ API for rendering geometry (triangle and quad meshes, curves,
spheres, boxes, planes, isosurfaces) and volumes (through Open VKL)
with ray casting, ambient occlusion, SciVis and path tracing
renderers, plus distributed rendering over MPI.  ParaView, VisIt and
OVITO use it as a rendering backend.
